.TH CHANGE_IP 8 "August 2026" "change_ip 2.6.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
change_ip \- make a provider-issued IPv4 the default outbound source
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B change_ip
.br
.B change_ip
.RB [ status | doctor | rollback ]
.br
.B change_ip
.I NEW_IP[/PREFIX]
.RI [ INTERFACE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Adds or reuses a provider-issued IPv4 address and makes it the explicit source
of the default IPv4 route. Existing addresses on the interface are kept.
.PP
The gateway and prefix must come from the hosting provider when the address is
not already configured. The script does not order addresses, open ports,
configure Docker, or configure a firewall.
.PP
On Debian and Ubuntu, persistence is a generated systemd oneshot service. It
runs after the network is online, adds the selected address, and restores the
selected gateway and source address. The script never reboots the machine
automatically.
.PP
With no arguments, an interactive wizard asks for the missing values.
.B status
shows the current source and persistence state.
.B doctor
checks the generated service.
.B rollback
restores the selected backup and the saved runtime route when available.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo change_ip
sudo change_ip status
sudo change_ip --dry-run 45.145.40.68/27 --gateway 45.145.40.65 -i enp1s0f0
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
ip(8), systemd(1), systemd-run(1)
